 34AR c  2020Ke03,2021Ke04: a 95-MeV {+24}Mg beam was produced from the ATLAS   
 34AR2c  accelerator at ANL and bombarded a |?200-|mg/cm{+2} {+12}C target.     
 34AR3c  Prompt |g rays were detected using the GRETINA tracking array          
 34AR4c  consisting of 12 modules. Fusion-evaporation residues were separated   
 34AR5c  and identified by the Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) with a focal-plane  
 34AR6c  position-sensitive parallel-grid avalanche counter (PGAC) and an       
 34AR7c  ionization chamber. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, recoil-|g(|q).       
 34AR8c  Deduced levels, J, |p. Compared with mirror nucleus {+34}S and shell   
 34AR9c  model calculations. Calculated astrophysical {+33}Cl(p,|g){+34}Ar      
 34ARAc  reaction rate and discussed its implications for the identification of 
 34ARBc  nova presolar grains from sulfur isotopic abundances.                  
